    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d140">

                <pb facs="0190" n="100" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1420</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-04-05T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 5, 1918,
                                4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>45. Your 61, April 2, 7 p.m. Both British and French made request sometime ago
                    which prompted statement to Japanese Government contained in Department’s No.
                    2108, dated March 11.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d140-f1"/> Department now has
                    assurance no action will be taken without full understanding with Allies or
                    United States Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
